  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1248 PM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nRain chances come back to the Coastal Plains on Monday afternoon as \nincreased moisture associated with an upper level inverted trough \nreaches the east Texas coast. The combination of increased moisture \nwith the seabreeze could bring isolated to scattered showers and \nisolated thunderstorms. By Tuesday afternoon, the upper level high \nshifts to the northeast into the middle Mississippi Valley and \nallows the local area to receive increased moisture from the Gulf as \nthe inverted trough pushes over South Central Texas. Medium range \nmodels and ensemble solutions are in good agreement that rain \nchances are limited for the next work week with the highest \nprobability (10 to 20 percent) over the Coastal Plains. As far as \nhigh temperatures for the work week, looking for above normal values \nranging from the mid to upper 90s and up to 102/103. Increased \nmoisture middle to late week could bring near to critical heat index \nvalues for areas along and east of the I-35 corridor and Coastal \nPlains.",
